# Where this project finds the Pixel Art drawing library.
#
#   cp pixelart.conf.example pixelart.conf   and edit.
#
# pixelart.conf is gitignored. The environment wins over it, so a one-off run can set the value
# inline instead.
#
# Same rule as harness.conf, for the same reason: point this at a PINNED RELEASE, never at the
# sibling checkout in ../PixelArt. This project does not build Pixel Art and does not read its
# sources. A checkout someone is working in can be mid-edit and uncompilable, and when that
# happened with the TestHarness it took a consuming project's tests down for reasons that had
# nothing to do with that project.
#
# The zip supplies both the assembly this mod compiles against and the mod the game loads, so
# those are the same bytes by construction.
#
# Keep it in step with the PixelArtVersion pin in src/ModEntry.cs. Pixel Art's 0.x API changes
# between minor versions, and the loader's dependencies carry no version constraint, so a mismatch
# otherwise surfaces as a MissingMethodException from somewhere unrelated.
#
#   https://github.com/sparr/atomcraft-mod-PixelArt/releases/tag/v0.4.0
#
PIXELART_ZIP="$HOME/.cache/atomcraft-pixelart-0.4.0/PixelArt.zip"

# The sha256 of PixelArt.zip as downloaded from that release. Verified on every run and fatal on
# a mismatch; empty skips the check. Pixel Art has published no SHA256SUMS yet, so this value is
# only as good as the download it was taken from -- from its next release take it from SHA256SUMS
# on the release page, which is the authority, rather than from a file already on disk.
PIXELART_ZIP_SHA256="eabbdbc3a6eeb8260558f2998f1e2901d2301a32caa49db506aa9bad9de0517d"
